./LOGBOOK.md:715:- OWNERSHIP: M2 exclusively owns relay bootstrap/session loss and one bounded relay-only reprobe while the current base stays healthy; it remains publicly connected/degraded and never sets provider reasserting. M3 exclusively owns path, host, route, mandatory/lane-pool, sleep/wake, NAT64, and captive reconnect. A current M3 event cancels M2 timers/attempts before any M3 retry loop begins.
./LOGBOOK.md:716:- GENERATION/PRIVACY: Runtime generation remains M1-owned, transport generation is M3-owned, and relay attempt/active generation is M2-owned. Association identity cannot cross that tuple. Schema-2 runtime/capability snapshots add finite reasons, retry owner, generations, and locally validated build/limit evidence while preserving explicit schema-1 responses; remote text and sensitive traffic identifiers remain structurally excluded.
