./LOGBOOK.md:744:- REVIEW/REVALIDATION: ADR-022 remains Proposed and every downstream consumer remains blocked pending independent architecture acceptance. Selected-SSH, physical-iPhone, HEV/OS/toolchain, relay, diagnostics, and policy drift are explicit revalidation triggers. Evidence: `.research/260721_task-260721-3miqh4-dns-runtime-policy-v1.md`, machine vectors and raw summaries under `.research/`, harness `scripts/dns-policy-evidence.py`.
./LOGBOOK.md:748:- DECISION: ADR-022 proposes one required ordered per-profile `dnsResolver` with a non-empty list of canonical numeric IPv4/IPv6 `dns53` endpoints and per-endpoint port default 53. There is no product/public-vendor default, hostname endpoint, physical resolver inheritance, exit-host shell discovery, DoH, or fake-DNS baseline. The earlier one-to-four endpoint ceiling and 5/5/15/10-second, 32/128-query values had no accepted evidence and are removed. New TASK-260721-3miqh4 owns measured endpoint/message/byte/capacity/timing defaults and hard caps; schema, transport, relay, and M4 consumers are blocked on its independently accepted `DNSRuntimePolicyV1`.
./LOGBOOK.md:750:- M2 BOUNDARY: An eligible client-UDP query gets at most one relay UDP attempt at the active endpoint. Only TC=1, pre-response size inability, UDP timeout, or typed relay failure permits M2 to request same-endpoint TCP; M1 then owns TCP reuse and later endpoint promotion. Structural work is one UDP plus at most one TCP attempt per configured endpoint under one injected deadline. Client TCP goes directly to M1; malformed/mismatched UDP does not select another resolver.
./LOGBOOK.md:751:- SAFETY/PLANNING: Resolver/policy validation and SSH `direct-tcpip` readiness precede route/DNS settings. Post-settings ordinary queries have only the virtual ingress -> authenticated SSH/relay -> explicit endpoint path. Endpoint exhaustion returns bounded SERVFAIL, withdraws safe-DNS capability, and clears settings; it cannot call the device resolver. Missing legacy resolver data yields `requiresResolverConfiguration` with no inferred migration. TASK-260721-33o8fc owns schema/codec/migration, TASK-260721-2raag7 owns M4 profile experience, and revised TASK-260715-5o6jqg/TASK-260715-28jdml/TASK-260715-336ljl own shared-failure, M2, and integration evidence.
./LOGBOOK.md:892:### 2158 — Shared relay hostile corpus is semantically identical in Swift and Go (TASK-260715-297gq6)
./LOGBOOK.md:896:- VERIFICATION: `make relay-protocol-check`, Go checkptr, Swift AddressSanitizer, strict Swift format, gofmt, Go vet, shell syntax, JSON validation, diff validation, and board validation pass. A five-second native Go fuzz run passed 1,453,381 executions with 19 new coverage-interesting inputs and no crash/invariant failure. Protocol source coverage is Swift 93.21% (1,797/1,928 lines) and Go 85.7% statements.
./LOGBOOK.md:897:- TOOLCHAIN: The repository still lacks the authoritative `relay/go.mod` and pinned Go 1.26.5 owned by TASK-260715-27uz4n, so local Go evidence uses the accepted standard-library-only `CGO_ENABLED=0` smoke under Go 1.25.5. This does not substitute for the later release-toolchain gate.
./LOGBOOK.md:899:### 2118 — Canonical relay v1 vectors use an independent deterministic oracle (TASK-260715-1q7u14)
./LOGBOOK.md:903:- TOOLCHAIN: The repository smoke harness remains intentionally pinned to the installed Go 1.25.5 because the authoritative `relay/go.mod` / Go 1.26.5 scaffold belongs to TASK-260715-27uz4n. The test is standard-library-only and `CGO_ENABLED=0`; release validation still requires the accepted 1.26.5 toolchain.
./LOGBOOK.md:909:- RESOLUTION: Swift and Go now validate ATYP, recomputed HDRLEN, address and port bounds, nonzero port, and exact outer/MSGLEN arithmetic before applying either payload limit. Mirrored tables cover every structural stage at both 513-byte local-policy and 1473-byte protocol-violation declarations with zero decoded materialization; valid 513-byte and 1473-byte records retain their distinct reject-versus-close outcomes. Verification: relay protocol gate, 150 Swift tests, Go vet/tests with 91.3% coverage, 1,135,854 fuzz executions, strict formatting, core-boundary guard, and diff validation all pass.
./LOGBOOK.md:913:- DECISION: The codec preserves HEV domain bytes as an opaque 1–248-byte wire value, including non-ASCII and NUL. DNS presentation-form, invalid A-label, raw-IP-text, and IDNA policy remains exclusively in the later Go resolution gate; neither codec normalizes, resolves, or logs domain bytes. The endpoint type is direction-neutral so a response encodes the relay-observed source rather than substituting the original destination.
./LOGBOOK.md:917:### 1847 — Incremental relay envelope codec is bounded and cross-language equivalent (TASK-260715-89h7cw)
./LOGBOOK.md:921:- REWORK: The Swift codec suite type is `RelayProtocolByteCodecTests`, so the frozen `swift test --filter RelayProtocol` step now selects it. `make relay-protocol-check` visibly runs the envelope suite and passes 29 tests across the generated-constants, handshake, and codec suites while retaining the mirrored Go smoke package.
./LOGBOOK.md:928:- COVERAGE: Swift `perform` tests now inject invalid/throwing writes, throwing reads, and EOF, assert stable code/phase mappings, and prove cancel/reset/close cleanup. Full validation passes: `make relay-protocol-check` (19 selected protocol tests), `swift test` (129/129), Go vet/test with `CGO_ENABLED=0` and 92.6% statement coverage, strict Swift format, gofmt, core-boundary check, `git diff --check`, and board validation.
./LOGBOOK.md:931:- IMPLEMENTATION: `RelayClientHandshake` drives the 12-byte client hello over the candidate-neutral `SSHByteChannel` with partial writes, fixed-size incremental reads, an injected deadline/cancellation seam, generation checks, and cancel/reset/close on failure. The Go relay uses a fixed `[ClientHelloWidth]byte` state machine and returns an explicit close action plus an exact 16-byte accepted or rejection hello.
./LOGBOOK.md:934:- VERIFICATION: 128 Swift tests pass, including 11 new handshake tests; the Go relay-protocol smoke vets/tests with `CGO_ENABLED=0` and the new package tests reach 92.1% statement coverage; strict Swift format, gofmt, core-boundary validation, schema/codegen drift checks, and `swift build` pass. Known scaffold constraint remains: `relay/go.mod` and pinned Go 1.26.5 validation belong to TASK-260715-27uz4n, so the accepted temporary smoke ran with workstation Go 1.25.5 as documented by TASK-260715-2azda7.
./LOGBOOK.md:937:- MILESTONE: One authority now generates both bindings: `Protocol/Relay/relay-v1.schema.json` → `scripts/relay-protocol-tool.py` → `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/RelayProtocol/Generated/RelayProtocolV1+Generated.swift` + `relay/internal/protocol/generated_v1.go` (checked in, runtime-parse-free). `make relay-protocol-generate` / `make relay-protocol-check` per the 111tde binding; all values verbatim from 111tde/18owh7. Ready for review.
./LOGBOOK.md:939:- DECISION: `relay/go.mod` NOT created — module scaffold stays with TASK-260715-27uz4n. `scripts/tests/test-relay-protocol-go.sh` compiles/vets/tests the package in a throwaway `.temp/` module (`GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, network-free). Workstation Go is 1.25.5; the pinned 1.26.5 is absent — module-pin verification remains with 27uz4n.
./LOGBOOK.md:941:- VERIFICATION: full gate PASS (double regen byte-identical, checked-in match, digest OK, stale/manual-edit self-test OK); live demo: hand-editing 1472→1473 in generated Go fails `check` exit 1; `swift test` 117/117; `check-core-boundaries` PASS. Evidence: board outcome `TASK-260715-2azda7_results.md`, demo diffs in `.temp/relay-protocol-demo/`.
./LOGBOOK.md:945:- VERIFICATION: Reviewer independently re-checked spec quotes (relay-protocol.md:110-113, security-privacy.md:59-66), HEV pinned-source bounds (`UDP_BUF_SIZE 1500` at hev-socks5-udp.c:26; stream-fatal `datlen > len − addrlen` at :203-206; `msgv[i].len = UDP_BUF_SIZE` in session-udp fwd_b → 1472 ≤ 1481 worst-case IPv6, reply write 1491 ≤ 1500 by construction), frame arithmetic (max legal body 1733 < floor 2048), reserved bit/type-range vacancy in the frozen binding, all 13 downstream ID-scoped notes, ADR-021 number vacancy, and diagram artifacts. No product code modified; `task-board validate` clean. Evidence: `.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-18owh7/TASK-260715-18owh7_review.md`.
./LOGBOOK.md:946:- NOTE for M3 (G1/G3): effective end-to-end mapping lifetime is min(client 60 s, relay 120 s) = 60 s — G3 must judge that effective value, not the relay timer alone; the 1472 "unfragmented egress" arm is IPv4 arithmetic (IPv6 would be 1452), the HEV bound is load-bearing.
./LOGBOOK.md:950:- DECISION: M0 uses fixed schema constants and unilateral local caps; nothing new on the wire beyond the existing `maxFrame` min-negotiation. Hello flag bit 1, feature bit 1, and message types `0x40–0x4F` reserved (unallocated) for an evidence-gated M3 limits exchange. Rationale: peer-advertised limits are unverifiable claims (local hard caps stay mandatory regardless), the datagram ceiling is HEV-pinned so negotiation has nothing to negotiate, and manifest-verified relay upload version-locks peer pairs. Full record: board outcome `TASK-260715-18owh7_decision.md`; awaiting review acceptance (proposed ADR-021).
./LOGBOOK.md:951:- FINDING: Pinned HEV caps UDP-in-TCP copy buffers at `UDP_BUF_SIZE = 1500` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:26`); `recvmmsg_tcp` returns `-1` (stream-fatal, not a drop) when `datlen > 1500 − addrlen` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:203-206`). With ADR-020 keeping HEV unmodified, the relay→client reply path physically cannot carry a UDP payload above 1481 bytes (IPv6). This, plus unfragmented 1500-MTU egress, fixes `maxUDPPayload = 1472` as a v1 wire constant; raising it is an HEV-fork decision, not a protocol negotiation.
./LOGBOOK.md:952:- DECISION: Baselines (all injectable, schema-owned floors/hard ceilings, fail-closed on out-of-range config): maxFrame [2048,65536] advertise 4096; maxAssociations 256 [1,1024]; per-assoc queue client 32KiB/relay 64KiB; aggregate/direction client 1MiB/relay 4MiB; control reserve 16/64KiB; DNS WRR 4:1; idle client 60s / relay 120s (RFC 4787 REQ-5 floor; client-first stagger shrinks crossed-expiry reopen race). `0x0005` split into violation (>1472, association-fatal) vs policy (lowered local cap, drop); `0x0006` edge-triggered per saturation episode.
./LOGBOOK.md:957:- MILESTONE: TASK-260715-111tde accepted → done. `TASK-260715-111tde_relay-binding-decision.md` is now the authoritative relay protocol v1 binding: schema/generated/handwritten ownership, deterministic regeneration + CI drift gates, bounded stream abstractions, dependency/license/FFI ceilings, and the full downstream consumer map. M2 protocol implementation (2azda7, 1y1g1u, 89h7cw, 516lhy, 1jvgcn, 1q7u14) is unblocked pending only the 18owh7 numeric-limit decision.
./LOGBOOK.md:958:- VERIFICATION: Wire contract byte-checked against `.spec/relay-protocol.md` (hello 12/16, envelope, message table, HEV payload — exact match); HEV `HDRLEN` 10/22/7+N and 248-byte domain cap confirmed via `.research/260720_pin-and-audit-hev-lwip-baseline.md:208-225`; SSH binding matches `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift:1480-1527`; toolchain/license ceilings match accepted 3bdplx; all 32 spot-checked consumer-map task IDs exist; A0/32umrc unlinked per override; `task-board validate` clean; no product code modified.
./LOGBOOK.md:963:- OVERRIDE / ROUTING: The reviewer-accepted task override supersedes the 1510 stop-line and deliberately decouples this reusable wire contract from Gate A0 and TASK-260715-32umrc. Binding authority is the accepted ReluxTunnelCore boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w), cgo-free Go 1.26.5 relay toolchain (TASK-260715-3bdplx), candidate-neutral SSHExecChannel (TASK-260720-100wu6), and ADR-005/006. The obsolete A0/32umrc dependency edges are removed; those decisions remain outside the relay contract.
./LOGBOOK.md:964:- DECISION: Canonical JSON at `Protocol/Relay/relay-v1.schema.json` generates checked-in Swift/Go values only; handwritten Swift in `ReluxTunnelCore/RelayProtocol` and Go in `relay/internal/protocol` own behavior. `make relay-protocol-generate` is the sole regeneration command and `make relay-protocol-check` owns deterministic double-generation, drift/manual-edit failure, compilation, and schema-negative gates. No Swift/Go FFI or runtime schema parser is permitted.
./LOGBOOK.md:965:- DECISION: Build identity uses a separate bounded `relux-relay --identity --protocol 1` exec record matched to the signed manifest before `--stdio --protocol 1`; the fixed 12/16-byte v1 hello remains unchanged and framed stdout stays uncontaminated. DNS priority is a negotiated scheduling hint only. HEV `MSGLEN` is DATA length, `HDRLEN` includes the three-byte prefix, and domain wire length is capped at 248 by one-byte `HDRLEN`.
./LOGBOOK.md:1098:### 2220 — Four relay assets built; native runtime and budget gates remain external (TASK-260715-24icoz)
./LOGBOOK.md:1099:- IMPLEMENTATION: Added `relay-portable-assets` / `inspect-assets`, which requires a caller-owned total bundle budget and emits a path-free four-asset report only after exact layout/name, regular executable mode, raw format/machine, Go CPU metadata, linkage, minimum runtime, dynamic-library, debug-section, size, SHA-256, and privacy checks. An over-budget report is retained before the command fails; no default budget silently creates product policy.
./LOGBOOK.md:1100:- VERIFICATION: A detached clean worktree at `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096` built exactly Darwin/Linux amd64/arm64 with pinned Go 1.26.5, `--require-clean`, release linker flags, protocol v1 identity `0.1.0`, and source epoch `1784656987`. The four files total 10,259,950 bytes and are retained in task outcome archive `TASK-260715-24icoz_portable-relay-assets.tar.gz`; each is mode 0755, stripped with no DWARF companion, and passed format/linkage/metadata/privacy inspection.
./LOGBOOK.md:1170:- MILESTONE: Go 1.26.5 relay toolchain decision reviewed and accepted; unblocks TASK-260715-1ccx3l, 1g9cyt, 32umrc and the M2 relay build with no open language/tooling question.
